# unit-watch-stall.vrs: unit-watch D25 (Session 1), the stall backstop and unstick in game. uw-stall (tools/vrclient/fixtures/
# uw-stall.json: uw-wave's shape, wave 1 of 4 CHAR_Spider_Forest, wave 2 of 2 waiting for its clear) at the mark uw-b, Chaos
# 150 m away and never fighting: no player within 40 m, so the standing rule never marks, and the spiders stand on open
# ground, so only the backstop does. "[nyar] unit-watch uw-stall stall: wave 1 quiet 1 min, 4 leftovers marked" comes
# 60-70 s after wave 1 queued (the clock starts at the first check after the wave is decided), then four "stuck: … (stall)"
# and four "recovered: … (player|group|anchor)" lines. Then uw-stall is restarted: `.nyar event unstick uw-stall` replies
# "unstick uw-stall: 4 units marked, 0 fighting left alone" and the twin `.nyar api event unstick uw-stall` (the same
# units, already marked, so marked=0) replies "[NYAR:ok] cmd=event verb=unstick id=uw-stall marked=0 fighting=0"; `.nyar
# event unstick nosuch` replies "unknown event nosuch", and an unstick of the stopped uw-stall "unstick uw-stall: not
# running". Every reply is screenshotted in real chat (profile probe 11.2).
#
# Needs: a Release DLL with unit-watch step 3; [UnitWatch] StallMinutes = 1 in the dev cfg for this run only (restored to 10
# after), Enabled = true, StuckSeconds 90; the dev events.json entry uw-stall (fixture above) enabled; NyarDevTools (.devtp,
# .devmark) and DevChatEcho; Chaos invulnerable (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, a Boolean, never false).
# Run: --var BX=-1580 --var BZ=-1640 (uw-b: hg-b, open ground in FarbaneWoods) --var FX=-1430 --var FZ=-1640 (150 m east)
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .devtp ${BX} ${BZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to x=(?P<PX>-?[0-9.]+) y=-?[0-9.]+ z=(?P<PZ>-?[0-9.]+)
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devmark uw-b
expect-log \[DEV MARK\] uw-b
chat .nyar event set uw-stall location here
expect-reply uw-stall location =
chat .devtp ${FX} ${FZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to x=(?P<QX>-?[0-9.]+) y=-?[0-9.]+ z=(?P<QZ>-?[0-9.]+)
expect-calc hypot(${QX} - ${PX}, ${QZ} - ${PZ}) >= 140
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-stall
expect-log event uw-stall started by manual timeout=20
expect-log event uw-stall wave 1/2 timeout=30
expect-no-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-stall stall: timeout=55
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-stall stall: wave 1 quiet 1 min, 4 leftovers marked timeout=20
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-stall stuck: CHAR_Spider_Forest wave 1 \(stall\) timeout=5
expect-seen \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-stall recovered: CHAR_Spider_Forest try 1/2, [0-9]+ m \((player|group|anchor)\) timeout=20
chat .nyar event info uw-stall
expect-reply unit watch: 4 stuck now, 4 recovered, 0 removed timeout=30
shot full uw-stall-info
# unstick on a fresh instance: the four new spiders have not fought
chat .nyar event stop uw-stall
expect-log event uw-stall stopped
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-stall
expect-log event uw-stall started by manual timeout=20
expect-log event uw-stall wave 1/2 timeout=30
wait 8
chat .nyar event unstick uw-stall
expect-reply unstick uw-stall: 4 units marked, 0 fighting left alone
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-stall stuck: CHAR_Spider_Forest wave 1 \(admin\)
wait 2
shot chat uw-unstick-reply
chat .nyar api event unstick uw-stall
expect-reply [NYAR:ok] cmd=event verb=unstick id=uw-stall marked=0 fighting=0
wait 2
shot chat uw-unstick-api
chat .nyar event unstick nosuch
expect-reply unknown event nosuch
wait 2
shot chat uw-unstick-nosuch
chat .nyar event stop uw-stall
expect-log event uw-stall stopped
chat .nyar event unstick uw-stall
expect-reply unstick uw-stall: not running
wait 2
shot chat uw-unstick-stopped
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
console TPHome
wait 3
